{"tool_name":"shapeit5","contents":["bioconda","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"shapeit5","version":"5.1.1","home":"https://odelaneau.github.io/shapeit5","documentation":"https://odelaneau.github.io/shapeit5","license":"MIT","summary":"Fast and accurate method for estimation of haplotypes (phasing).","identifiers":["doi:10.1101/2022.10.19.512867","biotools:shapeit5"],"description":"This package provides the software SHAPEIT5. SHAPEIT5 estimates haplotypes in large datasets (WGS, WES, SNP array), with a special focus on rare variants.","license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"number":2,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":[null,"make","cmake","clangdev"],"host":["boost-cpp","libcurl","libdeflate","bzip2","htslib","xz","zlib"],"run":["boost-cpp","htslib"]},"test":{"commands":["SHAPEIT5_phase_common --help","SHAPEIT5_phase_rare --help","SHAPEIT5_switch --help","SHAPEIT5_ligate --help"]}},"biotools":{"id":"shapeit5","home":"https://odelaneau.github.io/shapeit5/","license":"MIT","summary":"SHAPEIT5 is a software package to estimate haplotypes in large genotype datasets (WGS and SNP array).","addition_date":"2023-09-02T13:07:22.917482Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:41:52.021579Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["5.1.1"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:shapeit5","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"olivier.delaneau@unil.ch","name":"Olivier Delaneau","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3906-8446","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://odelaneau.github.io/lap-page"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://odelaneau.github.io/shapeit5/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence variations","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3498"},"format":[{"term":"BCF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3020"},{"term":"VCF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3016"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Phasing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3454"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence variations","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3498"},"format":[{"term":"BCF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3020"},{"term":"VCF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3016"}]}]}],"name":"SHAPEIT5","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"billsfriend","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41588-023-01415-w","metadata":{"abstract":"Phasing involves distinguishing the two parentally inherited copies of each chromosome into haplotypes. Here, we introduce SHAPEIT5, a new phasing method that quickly and accurately processes large sequencing datasets and applied it to UK Biobank (UKB) whole-genome and whole-exome sequencing data. We demonstrate that SHAPEIT5 phases rare variants with low switch error rates of below 5% for variants present in just 1 sample out of 100,000. Furthermore, we outline a method for phasing singletons, which, although less precise, constitutes an important step towards future developments. We then demonstrate that the use of UKB as a reference panel improves the accuracy of genotype imputation, which is even more pronounced when phased with SHAPEIT5 compared with other methods. Finally, we screen the UKB data for loss-of-function compound heterozygous events and identify 549 genes where both gene copies are knocked out. These genes complement current knowledge of gene essentiality in the human genome.","authors":[{"name":"Delaneau O."},{"name":"Hofmeister R.J."},{"name":"Ribeiro D.M."},{"name":"Rubinacci S."}],"citationCount":27,"date":"2023-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Genetics","title":"Accurate rare variant phasing of whole-genome and whole-exome sequencing data in the UK Biobank"},"pmcid":"PMC10335929","pmid":"37386248","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Population genetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3056"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"SHAPEIT5","home":"https://bio.tools/shapeit5","license":"MIT","version":"5.1.1","summary":"SHAPEIT5 is a software pack